Oneirodex schema migrations (Alembic)
=====================================

Adopted in the modernization program, wave A3.1. Supersedes the
"defer Alembic" decision in docs/adr/0001-schema-migrations-defer-alembic.md.

Layout
------
- alembic.ini        - config; sqlalchemy.url is intentionally blank
- env.py             - resolves the DB URL like the app (DATABASE_URL /
                       TEST_DATABASE_URL / config.Config, or `-x db_url=...`);
                       target metadata is oneirodex.models db.metadata
- versions/          - revision scripts; the first is the squashed baseline

Everyday use
------------
    # apply everything
    python -m alembic upgrade head

    # against an explicit database (no env vars touched)
    python -m alembic -x db_url=postgresql://user:pass@host/dbname upgrade head

    # new schema change: edit oneirodex/models.py, then
    python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"
    # review the generated script by hand before committing

    # drift gate (clean = metadata matches an upgraded DB)
    python -m alembic check

Do NOT add DDL to oneirodex/updateschema.py any more - it is frozen. It stays
only to carry pre-Alembic installs up to the baseline; init_manager stamps such
a database at the baseline revision on first boot after upgrade.

Known `alembic check` allow-list: docs/dev/alembic-baseline-notes.md
Operator upgrade steps: docs/runbooks/release-checklist.md
